  "BOUND_PROOFS": [
    "If U is the complement of kept coverage, i_U(B,C)>=i_full(B,C)-sum_R i_full(B,C,R). Each unconditional triple count is computed exactly from eight Venn-atom cardinalities. Common-number subset counts supply another lower bound L. Then iBC-iABC>=max(0,L-min(iAB,iAC)), proving the cheap pair upper bound. Every count and bound is integral.",
    "Every ticket is scored over all C(49,6) tickets. A ticket with r<F0-2*rho cannot appear in a triple reaching F0, because union<=sum(r)<=r+2*rho<F0. The threshold is mathematical, never fixed top-L.",
    "Every unordered triple has a unique smallest global-order anchor. Within its suffix, conditional sorting enumerates each remaining unordered pair exactly once.",
    "For fixed A, F(A,B,C)=r(A)+|res(B)\\res(A)|+|res(C)\\(res(A) union res(B))|<=r(A)+gA(B)+gA(C). The sum of the two largest remaining gA values bounds the whole block.",
    "Discarding a suffix ticket T requires r(A)+r(a+1)+r(T)<target; every other suffix ticket has r<=r(a+1), so no competitive pair involving T is lost.",
    "iABC<=min(iAB,iAC,iBC), so the retained pair bound remains admissible. Exact keys identify two colex ticket ranks; hash collisions cause replacement, never false reuse.",
    "All new pruning is strict (<target), preserving every optimum tie. Accounted blocks are disjoint. Closure requires their sum to equal C(13983816,3). Timeout includes the active conditional block and every later global anchor in its upper bound."
  ],
